1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 Nf6 4. d4 exd4 5. e5 Nd5 6. cxd4 Bb4+ 7. Nbd2 d6 8. Bb5 O-O 9. h3 dxe5 10. dxe5 Qe7 11. Bxc6 bxc6 12. O-O Ba6 13. Re1 Nf4 14. a3 Bxd2 15. Qxd2 Nd3 16. Re3 Rfd8 17. Qa5 Bc8 18. Bd2 Bf5 19. Bc3 c5 20. Rd1 Rd7 21. Rd2 c6 22. Qa6 Rad8 23. Qxc6 Be6 24. Qe4 Bd5 25. Qg4 Bxf3 26. gxf3 Qe6 27. Qh4 h6 28. Qe4 c4 29. f4 Nc5 30. Rxd7 Nxe4 31. Rxd8+ Kh7 32. Bb4 f5 33. Kf1 Qb6 34. Rd7 c3 35. bxc3 Qc6 36. Rxa7 Nd2+ 37. Ke2 Nc4 38. Rg3 Qe4+ 39. Re3 Qc2+ 40. Kf3 Qd1+ 41. Re2 Qd3+ $2 ({Aitken. 41...Nd2+ is a win. The white king gets caught in a mating net. One line is} 41... Nd2+ 42. Kg2 Qf1+ 43. Kh2 Nf3+ 44. Kg3 Ng1) 42. Re3 Nxe3 43. fxe3 Qf1+ 44. Kg3 Qg1+ 45. Kf3 Qf1+ 46. Kg3 Qg1+ {Source: Aitken Book 41. Scores: 1-4 D Parr, D Friedgood, E Brondum, J Hvenkilde 6/7... 13-24 JM Aitken, etc on 5.} 1/2-1/2

